no_token -> ✋ no token (run: brains.auth.set)
token_expired -> ✋ token expired (run: brains.auth.set)
needs_reauth -> ✋ stored token is stale — re-auth (run: brains.auth.set)
refresh_rejected -> ✋ refresh token dead (run: brains.auth.set)
refresh_server_error -> 💥 anthropic returned a server error — your token is fine; retry shortly
refresh_rate_limited -> 💥 rate-limited on token refresh — retry in a bit; if it never clears, the pinned user-agent (claude-code/2.0.1) may be stale — override with BRAINS_AUTH_UA
no_access_token -> 💥 refresh gave no access token — the oauth flow may have changed
refresh_curl_failed -> 💥 network error on token refresh — retry shortly
api_key_not_oauth -> ✋ that is an api key, not a subscription oauth token
keyrack_absent -> ✋ not stored yet (run: brains.auth.set)
keyrack_unreadable -> 💥 could not read the keyrack (run: rhx keyrack unlock --owner ehmpath --env prep)
active_token_expired -> ✋ live token expired — run any claude command to renew it
active_creds_unreadable -> 💥 could not read the live claude credentials
active_identity_unknown -> ✋ a login is present but unnamed — run any claude command, then retry
active_identity_unverified -> ✋ a login is present but its name could not be verified — run any claude command to renew it, then retry
curl_failed -> 💥 network error (see above) — retry shortly
rate_limited -> 💥 rate-limited — retry shortly; if it never clears, the pinned user-agent (claude-code/2.0.1) may be stale — override with BRAINS_AUTH_UA
unexpected_shape -> 💥 endpoint returned an unexpected shape — the api may have changed
usage_server_error -> 💥 anthropic returned a server error — your token is fine; retry shortly
usage_rejected -> ✋ the endpoint refused this token — it may lack the usage scope (re-run: brains.auth.set)
parse_failure -> 💥 could not read the endpoint response
some_code_we_never_declared -> 💥 some_code_we_never_declared
no_subscriptions -> ✋ no subscriptions stored yet — add one: brains.auth.set
keyrack_list_failed -> 💥 could not list the keyrack — unlock it: rhx keyrack unlock --owner ehmpath
